{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InvalidCapacity"],"anchor":"Destinations","title":"Destinations"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/batch(clock:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/deliver(to:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Delivery","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InvalidBatchBufferLimit","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/BufferDropReport"],"anchor":"Delivering","title":"Delivering"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination"},{"type":"text","text":" is a plain sink with one requirement, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which is given"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a batch of records, oldest first. Delivering is a chain of operators over a tracker’s records:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch()"},{"type":"text","text":" gathers them into batches of 20, and every 30 seconds while any are pending, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)"},{"type":"text","text":" makes a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Delivery"},{"type":"text","text":", which hands each batch to every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination. It holds a lazy unit of work, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Delivery\/work"},{"type":"text","text":", that runs once you call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"execute()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each destination receives its batches in order, one at a time, from a buffer of its own, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"slow one delays only itself. A full buffer drops its oldest batch and reports it as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/BufferDropReport","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" on the delivery’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Delivery\/bufferDropReports","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", which one task reads at a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time, as every report stream does. When the tracker has a store, the delivery reads the dropped","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch’s records back for that destination once it catches up, and tells the store when each batch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has reached every destination.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"What a destination receives is narrowed by modifiers: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)"},{"text":" for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consent categories it serves, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()"},{"text":", and added to by ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/enriched(by:)"},{"text":", which runs an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Enricher"},{"text":" on the records that destination alone receives. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"prints each event, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination"},{"text":" keeps the newest records it receives for the app to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read, in a debug view or a test.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Logs, traces and servers have destinations in modules of their own, so an app links only the ones"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it uses: "},{"code":"LoggerDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"code":"LoggingDestinations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SpanEventDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"TracingDestinations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"code":"HTTPDestinations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct Uploader: Destination {","    func receive(_ batch: [EventRecord]) async {","        \/\/ Send the batch, and return once it is somewhere it won't be lost.","    }","}","","let inspector = try InMemoryDestination(capacity: 500)","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records","    .batch(strategy: .count(20))","    .deliver(","        to: Uploader().accepting(.analytics).redactingSensitiveValues().droppingCallSite(),","        inspector","    )","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()","let received = inspector.events(of: SignedUp.self)  \/\/ [SignedUp(plan: \"pro\")]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The umbrella guide on this area is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Where tracked events go: the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Destination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol, the modifiers that narrow what a destination receives, and the delivery that hands it batches.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/destinations"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","externalID":"Destinations","modules":[{"name":"Destinations"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"Destinations"},"references":{"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations/Destination/receive(_:)":{"required":true,"type":"topic","title":"receive(_:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"receive"},{"kind":"text","text":"(["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EventRecord","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV"},{"ki